s are needed to supply the required 10 oxygen atoms.	 	C3H8 (g) +5O2   (g)  →  3CO2 (g) + 4H2O (l)Step 5 Verify that the number of atoms of each element is balanced in the final equation. The equation shows three carbon atoms, eight hydrogen atoms, and 10 oxygen atoms on each side.

